      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, looks professional. The parser gave it a decent initial rating, but it's still flagging it for \"low information density\" because the numeric count is relatively low. \n\nTo get this through the automated check, I need you to go much deeper. Please expand this into a full, comprehensive specification sheet for the entire unit. Don't just stick to the main rails—include detailed breakdowns for memory controller voltages, I/O timings, precise thermal dissipation coefficients at various loads, sub-percentage error rates for ECC, and granular power consumption metrics for every sub-block. \n\nThe goal is to have a massive amount of data points so the parser sees a high density of values. Make it as dense as possible so we don't have to keep revising it for the system.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
